# Cloudflare Pages security headers (Fable-5 audit A3, 2026-07-01).
# Motivation: BYOK provider keys live in localStorage — any XSS reads every
# user's key. The CSP is the blast-radius cut. Origins enumerated from the
# actual codebase; if a feature breaks with a CSP violation in console,
# extend the specific directive rather than removing the header.
#
# Per-origin rationale:
#   script-src   cdn.jsdelivr.net (MediaPipe tasks-vision) + youtube.com /
#                s.ytimg.com (iframe API) + wasm-unsafe-eval (MediaPipe WASM)
#   connect-src  generativelanguage.googleapis.com (BYOK Gemini direct —
#                Tier-1 key-blind path) + storage.googleapis.com (MediaPipe
#                model download) + cdn.jsdelivr.net (wasm fetch)
#   frame-src    self (operator preview iframe) + YouTube + Vimeo + Granicus meeting players
#   media-src    https: — per-city vendor MP4 hosts are arbitrary (Granicus,
#                Legistar variants); locking this breaks city players
#   img-src      YouTube thumbs + CartoDB/OSM map tiles + data:/blob: canvases
#                + *.googleusercontent.com (Google OAuth profile-picture avatars —
#                added 2026-07-04 after prod login showed a 404 placeholder where
#                localhost showed the real avatar; CSP was silently blocking).
#   style-src    unsafe-inline required (React style attributes + Vite)
#   Permissions-Policy: camera self-only (hand-tracking + /scan), mic/geo off
#   HSTS: 6-month max-age + includeSubDomains, no preload. Added per sol
#          pen-test Finding #14 as one authoritative source for HSTS at
#          the Pages layer. Cloudflare's own HSTS config (if any) should
#          be verified against this and made non-duplicative — the
#          browser tolerates multiple Strict-Transport-Security headers
#          by taking the first, but a single authoritative source keeps
#          config drift from becoming a silent security surface. No
#          `preload` directive on purpose: preload commits to HSTS
#          essentially forever (removal from browser preload lists is
#          slow); revisit only after a sustained public run with no
#          need to roll back.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://www.youtube.com https://s.ytimg.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://i.ytimg.com https://*.basemaps.cartocdn.com https://tile.openstreetmap.org https://*.googleusercontent.com; connect-src 'self' https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com https://storage.googleapis.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; media-src 'self' blob: https:; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://*.granicus.com; worker-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(self), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=15552000; includeSubDomains
